#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088554} :activity/id #uuid "08de5d22-7723-5283-ac76-b0a9c54b4ea9" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048293} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088554 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088904 :tutorial/content "We can draw a curve by defining a relationship between $x$ and $y$ using a third parameter $t.$ For example, suppose we have \n\n$$\nx=2t, \\,\\,\\, y=t^2, \\quad -3\\leq t\\leq 3.\n$$\n\nThese are the **parametric equations** of the curve.\n\nFirst, let's create a table for some values of $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x= 2t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y=t^2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nPlotting these points, we get the following curve:\n\n![](images/f7/f716e12c79731f363ace05965809bfc1963a6c3a231e1c4a96eaf3dbb62c848e.png)\n\nThe curve is actually a parabola.\nA curve defined by parametric equations is called a **parametric curve** and is said to be \"defined parametrically\"." :tutorial/id #uuid "f1327a56-c215-50cb-a30e-e43369078a3c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3349 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "218377cb-122a-56d3-9bc2-df2b7ebad88e" :step/math-academy-id 18547 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088555}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088555 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087717 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087518} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050790}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698142} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233325} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234248} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259554} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259555} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302271} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302273} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302274} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302275} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335959} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336019} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557627} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557631} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557649} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557666} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557674} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557680} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557691} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557694} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697642} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697645} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697653} {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218669